/T (The diagram shows the admission data of the application at the core, protected by successive layers. User permissions \(Read, Write and Admission_Officer_Access\) define what a user may do. Data sharing rules extend the visibility of records between roles or users at a chosen level of access. The role hierarchy of Principal, Admissions Head and Department Coordinator forms the outermost layer and influences which records each role can see. The key outcomes are controlled access to data, role-based visibility, safe collaboration through data sharing, and efficient administration.)
