257 0 obj
<<
/Title (Zoho Creator provides built-in mechanisms for managing users, roles, permissions and data visibility. In this experiment, the Read, Write and Admission_Officer_Access permissions of the Student Admission application were examined, the role hierarchy of Principal, Admissions Head and Department Coordinator was viewed, and a data sharing rule named Student_Admission_Form was configured to share the records of the Student Admission form from the Admissions Head role to the Department Coordinator role with Read Only access.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 186 0 R
/Next 258 0 R
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Title (The experiment shows how permissions, roles and data sharing work together so that each role sees the records it needs and no more. Choosing a suitable level of access, such as Read Only, allows records to be shared for collaboration without allowing them to be changed. Controlling who can access application data, and at what level, remains an essential part of building and managing business applications.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 186 0 R
/Prev 257 0 R
>>
